---
// Overview figure for "Slop Is Moving Up the Stack": where the slop lives. First the code itself, then iterating on it,
// now agents not understanding how their code will be used. Plain HTML so it follows the site theme.
---

<figure
  class="slop-overview not-prose"
  aria-label="Where agent slop lives. 2025: in the code itself, mostly fixed. Early 2026: in iterating on the code, improving. Now: agents not understanding how their code will be used, the core issue."
>
  <ol>
    <li class="better">
      <span class="when">2025</span>
      <b class="what">The code</b>
      <div class="art code" aria-hidden="true">
        <i></i><i></i><i class="bad"></i><i></i><i class="short"></i>
      </div>
      <p>Slop in the lines themselves: verbose checks, dead code, swallowed errors.</p>
      <span class="status">Mostly fixed</span>
      <span class="bench">SlopCodeBench rules</span>
    </li>
    <li class="better">
      <span class="when">Early 2026</span>
      <b class="what">Iterating on the code</b>
      <div class="art iterate" aria-hidden="true">
        <span><i></i><i class="fn" style="height: 10px"></i><i></i></span>
        <span><i></i><i class="fn" style="height: 22px"></i><i></i><i></i></span>
        <span><i></i><i class="fn" style="height: 40px"></i><i></i><i></i></span>
      </div>
      <p>Slop that piles up as the spec changes: functions that keep growing, structure that erodes.</p>
      <span class="status">Improving</span>
      <span class="bench">SlopCodeBench checkpoints</span>
    </li>
    <li class="worse">
      <span class="when">Now</span>
      <b class="what">How the code gets used</b>
      <div class="art use" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="lib"><em>library</em><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
        <span class="skip">✕</span>
        <span class="own"><em>agent's own copy</em><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
      </div>
      <p>Agents don't understand how code will be used: they rewrite libraries instead of using them, and write libraries other agents can't use.</p>
      <span class="status">The core issue now</span>
      <span class="bench">LibraryDesignBench</span>
    </li>
  </ol>
</figure>

<style>
  .slop-overview {
    --better: #2a78d6;
    --worse: #d4461c;
    --soft: color-mix(in srgb, var(--foreground) 62%, transparent);
    --line: color-mix(in srgb, var(--foreground) 14%, transparent);
    --ink-block: color-mix(in srgb, var(--foreground) 22%, transparent);
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
    color: var(--foreground);
  }
  :global(html[data-theme="dark"]) .slop-overview {
    --better: #4a94ec;
    --worse: #ee6a3d;
  }
  ol {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: none;
  }
  li {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 16px 18px 14px;
    border-top: 4px solid var(--tone);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--tone) 5%, transparent);
  }
  li + li {
    border-left: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  /* The arrow from one stage to the next. */
  li + li::before {
    content: "→";
    position: absolute;
    top: 14px;
    left: -11px;
    width: 22px;
    height: 22px;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    font-size: 14px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    color: var(--background);
    background: var(--foreground);
  }
  .better {
    --tone: var(--better);
  }
  .worse {
    --tone: var(--worse);
  }
  .when {
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--soft);
  }
  .what {
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--soft);
  }
  .status {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--tone);
  }
  .bench {
    margin-top: auto;
    padding-top: 6px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 700;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  /* Little drawings: code lines, a function growing across checkpoints, a library skipped for a copy. */
  .art {
    height: 64px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
  }
  .art i {
    display: block;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    background: var(--ink-block);
  }
  .code {
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 5px;
  }
  .code i {
    width: 75%;
  }
  .code i:nth-child(2) {
    width: 55%;
    margin-left: 12%;
  }
  .code i.bad {
    width: 62%;
    margin-left: 12%;
    background: var(--tone);
  }
  .code i.short {
    width: 35%;
  }
  .iterate {
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .iterate > span {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3px;
    width: 30%;
    padding: 4px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
  .iterate i.fn {
    background: var(--ink-block);
    outline: 2px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--foreground) 35%, transparent);
  }
  .use {
    gap: 8px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .use > .lib,
  .use > .own {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3px;
    width: 40%;
    padding: 4px 6px 6px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
  .use em {
    font-size: 10px;
    font-style: normal;
    color: var(--soft);
  }
  .use > .lib {
    opacity: 0.5;
  }
  .use > .own {
    border-color: var(--tone);
  }
  .use > .own i {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--tone) 45%, transparent);
  }
  .skip {
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--tone);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    ol {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
    li + li {
      border-left: 0;
    }
    li + li::before {
      content: "↓";
      top: -13px;
      left: 18px;
    }
  }
</style>
